 app/services/ffmpeg_convert_service.py
 Background FFmpeg video conversion — MP4 / H.264 / AAC / yuv420p.
 
-Design principles
-─────────────────
-• Runs ffmpeg in a subprocess on a daemon thread — never blocks the UI.
-• Uses utils.ffmpeg_locator to find ffmpeg regardless of platform or
-  bundle mode (PyInstaller / source / system PATH).
-• All paths are pathlib.Path objects; no hardcoded separators.
-• Output is written to ``<input_stem>_converted.mp4`` alongside the
-  source file so the original is never overwritten.
-• Progress is reported as a float 0.0–100.0 via an optional callback.
-• On completion or failure the ``on_done`` / ``on_error`` callback fires
-  on the same background thread — callers in the UI layer must marshal
-  to the main thread via ``widget.after(0, fn)``.
-
-Target format (fixed):
-  container : MP4
-  video     : H.264 (libx264), preset fast, CRF 22
-  audio     : AAC 192 kbps
-  pixel fmt : yuv420p   (guarantees broad player compatibility)
+iPhone-compatible presets
+──────────────────────────
+  high     : CRF 18, preset medium, 192k AAC, H.264 High@4.0  (lossless-ish)
+  standard : CRF 23, preset fast,   128k AAC, H.264 High@4.0  (default)
+  small    : CRF 28, preset fast,    96k AAC, scale ≤720p      (data saving)
+
+All presets use:
+  -pix_fmt yuv420p          broadest player compat (iPhone, Android, Windows)
+  -movflags +faststart       moov atom at front for instant playback
+  -vf scale=trunc…           force even dimensions (libx264 requirement)
+  -profile:v high -level 4.0 guarantees playback on every iPhone since 4S
 """
